=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  ports details ------------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Proposed: no Figma frame. System Details as root on the same$
# host: the Listening Ports section, after Host and IPs. A row$
# per socket, as ss lists them, in port order: port and$
# protocol, address, process. Read only, nothing about the$
# firewall.$
$
# System Details ###############################################$
$
  OS and Kernel ------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  OS                   Debian 13 (Trixie)$
   -  Kernel               6.12.113+deb13-cloud-amd64$
   -  Uptime               3 days, 5 hours, 12 minutes$
$
  Host and IPs -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Hostname             web-01$
   -  eth0                 192.0.2.20/24$
$
  Listening Ports ----------------------------------------------$
$
   -  22/tcp               0.0.0.0 sshd$
   -  22/tcp               [::] sshd$
   -  80/tcp               0.0.0.0 nginx$
   -  80/tcp               [::] nginx$
   -  443/tcp              0.0.0.0 nginx$
   -  443/tcp              [::] nginx$
   -  5353/udp             0.0.0.0 avahi-daemon$
   -  5432/tcp             127.0.0.1 postgres$
   -  5432/tcp             [::1] postgres$
   -  9090/tcp             192.0.2.20 prometheus$
   -  9100/tcp             * node_exporter$
$
  Users --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  alice                sudo$
$
  CPU and Load -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  CPUs                 2$
   -  Load                 0.08, 0.03, 0.01$
$
  Disk ---------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  /                    4.1 of 19.6 GiB (21%)$
$
  Memory -------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  RAM                  412 of 1968 MiB (21%)$
$
  Last Login ---------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  alice                2 hours ago from 192.0.2.10$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Refresh              Read the host again$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-1 or q]:$
$
$

